62
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:10,208
Oh. Lucy's free after all, see you.

63
00:04:11,293 --> 00:04:14,087
No, no, no, hey, hey, hey,
you can't leave, we just started.

64
00:04:14,296 --> 00:04:18,133
You're right, I should finish the game.
I take my plus-one long sword...

65
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:22,179
...stab myself in the face with it.
I'm dead, I've got a date with a girl. Bye.

66
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:25,307
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
We'll be fine. Watch.

67
00:04:25,474 --> 00:04:31,897
Ahem. Suddenly, a spectral shape rises from
Koothrappali's bloody corpse and says:

68
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:37,194
[MIMICS RAJESH] "Don't worry, buddies. Ghost
Raj will help guide you through the forest."

69
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:43,742
[MIMICS NICHOLAS CAGE] I'm just a tree,
but if I were you, I'd listen to your ghost friend.

70
00:04:48,038 --> 00:04:50,081
Go on. Give him your lunch money.

71
00:04:55,212 --> 00:04:57,339
I'm very happy you were able to hang out.

72
00:04:57,506 --> 00:04:58,799
Me too.

73
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:02,677
Not that it's up to you to make me happy.
Unless you find neediness sexy...

74
00:05:02,886 --> 00:05:05,806
...in which case you're with
the hottest man on the planet. Heh.

75
00:05:08,350 --> 00:05:09,810
Can I tell you something?

76
00:05:09,976 --> 00:05:11,686
I was so nervous about seeing you...

77
00:05:11,895 --> 00:05:16,149
...before I left my apartment, I put roll-on
antiperspirant all over my body.

78
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:17,692
-Really?
-Yeah.

79
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:20,987
If sweat starts squirting out
the top of my head, you'll know why.

80
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:24,241
I'm sorry to put you through that.

81
00:05:24,825 --> 00:05:28,495
It's okay. I'm trying to force myself
to do things that make me scared.

82
00:05:28,662 --> 00:05:30,872
What else have you been
thinking about doing?

83
00:05:31,122 --> 00:05:32,290
Well, let's see.

84
00:05:32,457 --> 00:05:36,086
I'd love to be able to tell the lady
who cuts my hair that I don't like bangs.

85
00:05:38,088 --> 00:05:40,757
-I like your bangs.
-Thanks, I like them too.

86
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,394
-What else?
-Hmm.

87
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:55,397
It's a tie between sending food back
in a restaurant...

88
00:05:55,564 --> 00:05:58,233
...and saying no to kids
who sell magazines door to door.

89
00:05:59,109 --> 00:06:00,235
Those are both toughies.

90
00:06:00,402 --> 00:06:02,988
I know. I have a two-year subscription
to Guns and Ammo.

91
00:06:06,365 --> 00:06:10,537
I push my shoulder against
the secret door to see if it gives way.

92
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:12,956
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
Uh-huh. It does.

93
00:06:13,123 --> 00:06:14,165
[MIMICS DOOR CREAKING]

94
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,961
He does sound effects too.

95
00:06:19,421 --> 00:06:21,673
Hey, I always did sound effects.

96
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:25,218
Uh, a swarm of bloodthirsty bats
fly through the dungeon.

97
00:06:25,384 --> 00:06:26,428
[MIMICS BATS SUCKLING]

98
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:31,308
Uh, uh, they attack a nearby unicorn.

99
00:06:31,474 --> 00:06:32,517
[MIMICS UNICORN GROANING]

100
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:35,228
[MIMICS BATS SUCKLING]

101
00:06:37,314 --> 00:06:40,233
Okay, well, I have a sound effect
for those sound effects.

102
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:41,526
[BLOWS RASPBERRY]

103
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:46,489
-Guess who?
-What are you doing back?

104
00:06:46,698 --> 00:06:48,825
That's an excellent question. Amy?

105
00:06:49,868 --> 00:06:51,286
Uh, well...

106
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:56,415
...when we were going through security,
I got pulled out of line for a pat-down.

107
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:59,836
The, uh, TSA agent got a little handsy.

108
00:07:01,004 --> 00:07:03,924
I may have broken her nose
with my elbow.

109
00:07:05,592 --> 00:07:07,677
Long story short, she's on the no-fly list...

110
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:10,263
...and we might have been
followed here by a drone.

111
00:07:11,389 --> 00:07:15,685
-I'm sorry. I feel like such an idiot.
-Oh, it's not so bad. You lost money...

112
00:07:15,852 --> 00:07:20,523
...you're filled with shame, you got groped
by a stranger. That's Vegas, you nailed it.

113
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:25,111
You guys enjoy your evening. I'm gonna go
before I ruin anybody else's weekend.

114
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,656
That's my girl.

115
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:32,911
Amy, wait. I know it's not the night
you had in mind...

116
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:35,372
...but why don't you stay and play?
It'll be fun.

117
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:36,873
Fun?

118
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:39,376
Three weeks ago you bought
crunchy peanut butter...

119
00:07:39,542 --> 00:07:43,171
...now you want the girls to play D&amp;D
with-- Do you have a drug problem?

120
00:07:44,047 --> 00:07:47,425
What's the big deal? Raj bailed,
so we could use some extra players.

121
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:50,637
I've just never played
Dungeons &amp; Dragons with girls before.

122
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:53,348
Oh, don't worry, sweetie. No one has.

123
00:07:56,685 --> 00:07:57,936
So, what do you say?

124
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:02,065
I'll leave it up to the Dungeon Master.

125
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:09,614
A satanic fungus that looks suspiciously
like Al Pacino...

126
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:13,201
...rises from the forest floor and says:

127
00:08:13,410 --> 00:08:15,245
[MIMICS AL PACINO]
"You're playing D&amp;D...

128
00:08:15,954 --> 00:08:17,580
...you're playing D&amp;D...

129
00:08:17,789 --> 00:08:20,291
...this whole apartment...

130
00:08:22,419 --> 00:08:24,212
...is playing D&amp;D."

131
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:33,013
Okay, who wants a drink?

132
00:08:33,221 --> 00:08:36,933
Penny, we don't consume alcohol during
Dungeons &amp; Dragons.

133
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:39,561
It impairs our judgment.

134
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:44,232
Oh, this isn't alcohol.
It's a magic potion that makes me like you.

135
00:08:47,819 --> 00:08:49,612
Double potion, please.

136
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:51,698
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
Here we go.

137
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:57,662
You find yourselves face to face
with two hulking ogres.

138
00:08:57,871 --> 00:09:00,832
[IN DEEP VOICE]
"What are you doing in our dungeon?"

139
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:04,794
"You shall die."

140
00:09:06,838 --> 00:09:09,215
Okay, literal goosebumps. Look.

141
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:13,053
-[IN NORMAL VOICE] What do you do?
-I draw my broadsword.

142
00:09:13,470 --> 00:09:16,473
-I ready my quarter-staff.
-I drink my potion.

143
00:09:19,142 --> 00:09:22,103
-I say we attack the big one.
-Give me the dice. I wanna roll.

144
00:09:22,312 --> 00:09:24,272
The Dungeon Master's supposed to roll.

145
00:09:24,439 --> 00:09:28,151
Yeah, well, I'm supposed to be in Vegas
throwing up on a shrimp buffet, give it.

146
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:33,948
-All right, what do I need?
-Uh, fifteen or higher.

147
00:09:34,157 --> 00:09:38,453
Fifteen's the point. The point is 15. Give the
little lady some room. Here it is. Coming out.

148
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:41,915
-Sixteen! Yeah.
-Yeah.

149
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:45,794
Please tell me we're playing for money.

150
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:50,048
Oh, even better than money.
You gained experience points.

151
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:53,676
-More potion, please.
-Yeah.

152
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:58,598
-How are your crab cakes?
-Kind of funky.

153
00:09:58,765 --> 00:10:00,558
-That's great.
-It is?

154
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:03,103
Does "funky" mean
something different in India?

155
00:10:04,187 --> 00:10:08,733
No, no. You've always wanted to send your
food back in a restaurant. Here's your chance.

156
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:12,445
-That's okay. I just won't eat them.
-Don't be ridiculous. Waiter?

157
00:10:13,947 --> 00:10:15,156
Everything all right?

158
00:10:16,241 --> 00:10:20,161
Uh, yeah. Everything all right with you?

159
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:21,371
Yes.

160
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:25,208
-Okay, thanks, bye.
-Hold on.

161
00:10:26,126 --> 00:10:27,961
Isn't there something else
you wanted to tell him?

162
00:10:29,546 --> 00:10:34,843
No, it's fine. He's from a different country.
He doesn't understand our ways.

163
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:38,847
Don't be silly. Just tell him.

164
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:44,269
I have to go to the bathroom. And it's not
because the crab cakes are funky.

165
00:10:46,688 --> 00:10:50,692
-So you're okay here?
-Uh, yeah, sorry. She's just a little shy.

166
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,236
The first time we met, she was so nervous...

167
00:10:53,403 --> 00:10:55,864
...she climbed out
a bathroom window to get away.

168
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:12,589
Uh-oh.

169
00:11:17,385 --> 00:11:18,761
Hey, Raj?

170
00:11:19,345 --> 00:11:20,889
Funny story.

171
00:11:22,891 --> 00:11:25,602
Come on, Mama wants
a pair of dead ogres.

172
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:28,813
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
Seventeen! The larger ogre is dead.

173
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:30,023
[ALL CHEERING]

174
00:11:30,773 --> 00:11:32,442
The other ogre says:

175
00:11:32,609 --> 00:11:34,527
[IN DEEP VOICE]
"You killed my brother."

176
00:11:35,862 --> 00:11:38,740
"Now Ogre Thanksgiving is ruined."

177
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:44,120
That is amazing.
He made me care about the ogre.

178
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:48,082
All right, Amy, there's one ogre left.
Take him out.

179
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:50,877
-Okay.
-Pretend he's that TSA agent. Come on.

180
00:11:53,338 --> 00:11:54,756
Nineteen.

181
00:11:54,923 --> 00:11:55,965
[ALL CHEERING]

182
00:11:57,592 --> 00:12:01,720
-This is turning out to be better than Vegas.
-Ha, ha. No, it's not.

183
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:06,643
Lucy?

184
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,854
Hey, long time no see.

185
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:15,944
You don't know me very well,
but each time you crawl out a window...

186
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:18,737
...to escape my company,
it chips away at my masculinity.

187
00:12:20,615 --> 00:12:23,034
-I'm sorry.
-Why would you leave like that?

188
00:12:23,201 --> 00:12:25,870
You were pushing me.
I didn't want to send my food back...

189
00:12:26,037 --> 00:12:27,580
...and you tried to make me do it.

190
00:12:27,746 --> 00:12:31,084
If I upset you,
why didn't you say something?

191
00:12:31,251 --> 00:12:34,128
How can I tell you I'm upset
if I can't tell the woman at Supercuts...

192
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:36,089
...that my forehead's my best feature?

193
00:12:38,216 --> 00:12:42,845
-It's scary.
-Well, I like you a lot and that's scary for me.

194
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:45,473
Mostly because you're a proven flight risk.

195
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:49,768
How could you like me a lot?

196
00:12:50,812 --> 00:12:54,899
Well.... For one thing, you have
bigger emotional problems than I do...

197
00:12:55,066 --> 00:12:57,443
...and I find that very attractive in a woman.

198
00:12:59,404 --> 00:13:01,114
I don't know, I just....

199
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:04,409
I think you're wonderful.

200
00:13:11,958 --> 00:13:13,584
I'm sweating out of my head.

201
00:13:17,839 --> 00:13:22,593
[IN NORMAL VOICE] The dragon falls
from the sky, crashing into the volcano.

202
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:23,845
[ALL CHEERING]

203
00:13:24,512 --> 00:13:26,764
But wait, he's not dead.

204
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:32,353
He crawls out, spreads his wings
and prepares to attack--

205
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:34,188
Wait.

206
00:13:35,648 --> 00:13:38,026
Doesn't he say something first?

207
00:13:38,192 --> 00:13:41,863
Maybe in the voice of a beloved celebrity?

208
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:43,990
Fine.

209
00:13:44,157 --> 00:13:47,201
[MIMICS CHRISTOPHER WALKEN]
"You'd think, after all these years...

210
00:13:47,702 --> 00:13:51,539
...I'd know not to fly over volcanoes.

211
00:13:53,875 --> 00:13:55,251
I'm a frigging idiot."

212
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:01,924
The dragon's Christopher Walken. Perfect.

213
00:14:02,091 --> 00:14:05,219
Amy, it's your turn.
We need one more hit. Finish him off.

214
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:07,846
Here we go. Fifteen.

215
00:14:08,014 --> 00:14:10,308
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
It's a hit, the dragon collapses to the ground.

216
00:14:10,475 --> 00:14:13,061
Wait, wait.

217
00:14:13,227 --> 00:14:15,229
And says....

218
00:14:17,106 --> 00:14:20,401
[MIMICS CHRISTOPHER WALKEN]
"Mother? Is that you?

219
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:25,615
Your little boy is coming home."

220
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:32,705
I don't know about you guys, but I've been
through the emotional wringer tonight.

221
00:14:33,081 --> 00:14:38,002
This may be the potion talking, but you are
one fine-ass Dungeon Master.

222
00:14:38,169 --> 00:14:41,381
[IN NORMAL VOICE] When we get home,
I'm gonna take you on a different adventure.

223
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:46,052
Another quest by Wolowitz?
Count me in.

224
00:14:47,929 --> 00:14:52,225
-Sheldon, they're talking about sex.
-Oh, then I'm out.

225
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:56,396
Ooh, I have an idea.

226
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:58,189
Since it's not happening
